From 13fd3849ceff4f8d42327149ecdbb853b139673a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:12:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Damoov Android SDK integration (Phase 2, not yet
 activated)

Adds react-native-telematics and the native/config layer needed to build
it into the Expo-managed Android project: expo-build-properties overrides
(compileSdk 37, Kotlin 2.3.21, Damoov's Maven repo) and a small config
plugin removing android:allowBackup, plus the two extra manifest
permissions Damoov's own integration guide requires. Validated with a
real `expo prebuild --platform android` against a scratch copy of this
exact repo state before committing -- confirmed Expo 57/RN 0.86's actual
defaults (minSdk 24, targetSdk 36, AGP 8.12.0, Gradle 9.3.1) already
match Damoov's requirements with no override, autolinking correctly
discovers the package end-to-end, and none of the existing config
plugins or permissions regressed.

Adds a thin src/lib/damoov/telematicsSdk.ts re-export and
useDamoovTelemetry.ts, a driver-tab lifecycle hook mirroring
useAutoTripTracking's active-rental-gated start/stop and dual-role
teardown safety net. Wires the three listeners with a documented,
verified event schema (location, tracking-state, speed-violation) into
telematics_live_status/telematics_events, and upserts
driver_telematics_accounts through the SDK's own init -> device id ->
permission wizard -> enable -> start-tracking sequence.

The hook is NOT mounted into the driver layout yet -- deliberately left
inactive pending Damoov InstanceId/InstanceKey native configuration,
which this package's own docs don't expose a JS-level API for and which
needs Damoov's Android integration guide (docs.damoov.com, unreachable
from this environment) to resolve correctly. Mounting it before that's
confirmed risks a real SDK-init failure path for every driver on the
next build.

Also fixes a Phase 1 bug: the four telematics_* tables' driver_id
columns pointed at driver_profiles.id, but every existing table with a
driver_id column (applications, vehicle_trips, driving_events)
references profiles.id instead -- the id every RLS policy and app query
already treats as auth.uid(). Corrected directly on the Supabase project
(all four tables were still empty) and regenerated types to match.

Zero changes to any AI Inspection file, table, or edge function --
confirmed via diff against HEAD before and after this commit.
